{
  "id": "fluency-l3-strange-powers",
  "course": "exp-log",
  "lesson": "l3-strange-powers",
  "title": "Fluency: powers that are fractions or negative",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "negative-power",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "work out a negative power",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [2, 30] },
        "n": { "int": [1, 3] }
      },
      "let": { "an": "a^n", "key": "1/a^n", "big": "a^n", "times": "-a*n" },
      "where": ["a^n <= 1000"],
      "prompt": "Work out ${a}^{{-{n}}}$. Give a fraction or a decimal.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{key}", "tol": { "rel": 0.002 }, "placeholder": "fraction or decimal", "accept": "${key:frac}$, or a decimal within 0.2%" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "dropped-minus", "value": "{big}", "tol": { "rel": 0.002 }, "line": "You dropped the minus: ${a}^{{-{n}}}$ is one over ${an}$, not ${an}$ itself." },
        { "id": "times-the-power", "value": "{times}", "tol": { "rel": 0.002 }, "line": "You multiplied {a} by ${-n}$: a power is not a product with the base." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "A negative power means one over the positive power.",
        "So ${a}^{{-{n}}} = {key:frac}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fractional-power",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "work out a fractional power",
      "vars": {
        "r": { "int": [2, 10] },
        "n": { "int": [2, 3] },
        "m": { "int": [1, 3] },
        "g": { "pick": [1, -1] }
      },
      "let": { "a": "r^n", "s": "g*m", "key": "r^(g*m)", "times": "r^n*g*m/n", "flip": "r^(-g*m)" },
      "where": ["gcd(m, n) == 1", "times != key"],
      "prompt": "Work out ${a}^{{{s}/{n}}}$. Give a fraction or a decimal.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{key}", "tol": { "rel": 0.002 }, "placeholder": "fraction or decimal", "accept": "${key:frac}$, or a decimal within 0.2%" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "times-the-power", "value": "{times}", "tol": { "rel": 0.002 }, "line": "You multiplied {a} by the power: a fraction in the power takes a root, not a share of {a}." },
        { "id": "flipped", "value": "{flip}", "tol": { "rel": 0.002 }, "line": "Check the sign of the power: a minus means one over, and no minus means no flip." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "${a}^{{1/{n}}} = {r}$: {n} equal steps, each multiplying by {r}, take 1 up to {a}.",
        "The top of the power, ${s}$, counts those steps; a minus counts them downwards, dividing.",
        "So ${a}^{{{s}/{n}}} = {key:frac}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "laws-then-evaluate",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "use the index laws, then evaluate",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [2, 5] },
        "m": { "int": [-4, 7], "not": [0, 1] },
        "n": { "int": [-4, 7], "not": [0, 1] },
        "k": { "int": [-3, 0] }
      },
      "let": { "t": "m + n", "p": "m + n - k", "key": "a^k", "added": "a^(m + n + p)", "multiplied": "a^(m*n - p)" },
      "where": ["p != 0", "p != 1", "abs(p) <= 9", "a^(-k) <= 125", "m*n != m + n", "m + n + p != m*n - p", "abs(m*n - p) <= 40", "abs(m + n + p) <= 40"],
      "prompt": "Work out $\\dfrac{{{a}^{{{m}}} \\times {a}^{{{n}}}}}{{{a}^{{{p}}}}}$. Give a fraction or a decimal.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{key}", "tol": { "rel": 0.002 }, "placeholder": "fraction or decimal", "accept": "${key:frac}$, or a decimal within 0.2%" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "added-the-bottom", "value": "{added}", "tol": { "rel": 0.002 }, "line": "Dividing subtracts powers: take away ${p}$, do not add it." },
        { "id": "multiplied-the-top", "value": "{multiplied}", "tol": { "rel": 0.002 }, "line": "Multiplying adds powers: ${m} + {n:()} = {t}$, not ${m} \\times {n:()}$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "On top, add the powers: ${m} + {n:()} = {t}$.",
        "Dividing subtracts: ${t} - {p:()} = {k}$, so the value is ${a}^{{{k}}}$.",
        "${a}^{{{k}}} = {key:frac}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "power-of-a-power",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "write a power of a power as one power",
      "vars": {
        "m": { "int": [-5, 6], "not": [0, 1] },
        "n": { "int": [-3, 4], "not": [0, 1] },
        "p": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0, 1] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "mn": "m*n", "key": "m*n - p", "added": "m + n - p", "plus": "m*n + p" },
      "where": ["m + n != m*n", "m*n != 1", "m + n - p != m*n + p"],
      "prompt": "Write $\\dfrac{{\\left({v}^{{{m}}}\\right)^{{{n}}}}}{{{v}^{{{p}}}}}$ as a single power ${v}^k$. What is $k$?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{key}", "tol": { "abs": 0 }, "placeholder": "a whole number" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "added-the-powers", "value": "{added}", "tol": { "rel": 0.002 }, "line": "A power of a power multiplies: $\\left({v}^{{{m}}}\\right)^{{{n}}} = {v}^{{{mn}}}$." },
        { "id": "sign-of-divide", "value": "{plus}", "line": "Dividing subtracts powers: take away ${p}$, do not add it." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "A power of a power multiplies: ${m} \\times {n:()} = {mn}$.",
        "Dividing subtracts: ${mn} - {p:()} = {key}$, so $k = {key}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
